window.FWN_SHADOW_SLAVE_CHAPTERS=(window.FWN_SHADOW_SLAVE_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":3201,"title":"Chapter 3201 A Land Without Monsters","paragraphs":["The city was vast and prosperous, built with not only utility in mind, but beauty as well. That was why the city lord's stronghold resembled a temple more than a fortress, with marble pillars supporting carved pediments and exquisite statues watching over the verdant gardens. That was not to say that it wasn't a fortress, though — just from one glance, Shadow could see how easy it was to defend.","The soldiers escorted him and Noctis to the heart of the stronghold, where a great reception hall rested in the shadows, radiant beams of sunlight spilling through high windows.","There, they met a placid man who looked to be in his thirties, wearing a simple white tunic and an azure toga. His auburn hair spilled to his shoulders, supported by a golden band, and his eyes were both enlightened and clear.","Despite how young the man looked, Shadow could feel the weight of wisdom in his gaze — a wisdom that could only be earned by living a long life and experiencing many things. Even without peering into the man's soul, he knew that the lord of the city was a Transcendent who had weathered hundreds of years.","Noctis had called him an old man, after all... granted, all men seemed old to that inexperienced youth.","Speaking of Noctis, the closer they came to the city lord's stronghold, the more nervous he looked. Now that they stood directly in front of the lord, there were beads of sweat rolling down his face.","Despite that, the lord himself seemed calm enough. If anything, his faint smile looked friendly.","“Welcome, Beast of Twilight... and his friend.\"","The lord's gaze lingered on Shadow for a few moments, then moved on. He probably guessed that the young man accompanying Noctis was not a mundane person, but chose not to question his identity just yet. Noctis remained silent for a few moments, then gave the lord an awkward bow.","\"Beast of Twilight greets Arelen, the Altar Sage.\"","Then, he cleared his throat and forced out a few more words.","\"Listen, Lord Arelen... about the last time... it was all a misunderstanding! Let me explain myself?\"","Shadow spared him a brief glance, amused by the spirited youth's sudden docility. It seemed he still knew how to respect his elders, at least.","The city lord — Transcendent Arelen, seemingly known as the Altar Sage — just chuckled and waved a hand dismissively.","“No need to explain. It's all in the past... a small matter.\"","He clasped his hands behind his back and walked toward Noctis and Shadow, giving the soldiers a nod to leave.","“Rather, I simply invited you here to have a welcoming feast and perhaps discuss a few matters. I couldn't let an honored guest stay at an inn, could I? So, please, follow me.\"","Noctis seemed quite surprised by Arelen's amicable attitude. He glanced at Shadow nervously, and once the ruler of the city walked past them, leaned closer to whisper:","\"I don't like this, Shadow! If something happens, let's bolt!\"","Shadow simply shrugged, turning to follow their host.","Despite the worries of the young Transcendent, Lord Arelen was true to his word. Soon enough, they arrived at a hall where a lavish feast had already been prepared. As they enjoyed the food, musicians played soft melodies, and nimble dancers performed a beautiful dance in front of them.","The atmosphere was harmonious, as if there was no bad blood between Arelen and Noctis, and as if the city outside was not drowning in a strange tension.","The Altar Sage inquired about the journey Noctis had undertaken, showing a hint of curiosity.","\"So, Noctis, how have you fared in your recent travels? I heard that you ventured to discover the source of the dreadful darkness that had devoured the Shadow people. Were you successful in eliminating that ancient curse?\"","Noctis let out a nervous laugh.","He glanced briefly at Shadow, then said:","\"Well... the darkness is gone now, and sunlight washes over the bones of those poor folks once again. So, one could say that this humble hero was a little bit successful. However, only ruins and desolation remain in that land, while beyond the ruins, the forests are teeming with terrifying horrors. The curse is gone, but... uh... I wouldn't say that I vanquished it. I just happened to be lucky.\"","The Altar Sage seemed a little surprised.","\"The darkness is gone? What a great achievement! For generations, many outstanding heroes had attempted to liberate that distant realm from its clutches. None had succeeded, yet you managed to destroy it alone. Truly a feat worthy of Noctis, the Beast of Twilight!\"","Noctis smiled weakly.","\"Y—yes... truly a feat worthy of me! Let's not talk about it anymore, though. You're making me feel shy.\"","Shadow was pretty sure that there wasn't a shy bone in the young wastrel's body, but he chose to stay silent.","Not long after that, though, he finally spoke for the first time. Turning to the ruler of this land, he asked:","\"On the way here, we noticed that the streets of your city are unusually crowded, Lord Arelen. People huddle in makeshift tents and wear anxious expressions. If I may ask, has something unfortunate transpired?\"","He had a feeling that the tense atmosphere of the city was the real reason why the Altar Sage had invited Noctis to come, and even seemed to forgive his past transgressions. If anything, it looked like Arelen wanted to placate Noctis, for whatever reason.","So, everything they had talked about until now was merely a preamble to the real conversation.","The Altar Sage remained silent for a few moments, looking at Noctis and Shadow with a faint smile, then sighed.","His smile slowly drained away.","\"Indeed, something unfortunate has happened. I am afraid that my lands will be attacked quite soon, so the people of the surrounding towns and villages were forced to seek shelter behind its walls.\"","Noctis almost spat his wine and stared at the older Transcendent, surprised.","“Attacked? What kind of abomination has crawled out of its den, and how powerful must it be for all the people of your land to flee?\"","The Creature of Corruption had to be extremely fearsome, considering that a powerful and experienced Transcendent like the Altar Sage had not gone out to battle it. If it was too strong for a single Transcendent to defeat... that could explain why Arelen was being so friendly to Noctis, who was a fierce warrior despite his young age.","Shadow took a sip of his wine, savoring its flavor. He had never tasted wine before — not in this lifetime, at least — and was finding its rich bitterness, brightened by a hint of sweetness, quite refreshing.","‘If it's just a Creature of Corruption, there is no need for concern.'","However, the long silence of the Altar Sage made him frown slightly.","He had a feeling that matters were not that simple, after all.","Eventually, Arelen slowly shook his head.","\"There is no abomination, young Noctis. Instead, it is Lady Irian, the Blade of Dawn, who has assembled an army to besiege my city and lay claim to my lands.\"","Noctis looked stunned.","He remained silent for a long while, as if struggling to understand what the Altar Sage had said. Finally, he let out a bewildered laugh.","“You must be joking, Lord Arelen. Isn't Lady Irian known for her valor, wisdom, and virtue? And aren't the two of you old comrades who have battled countless Creatures of Corruption side by side? Everyone knows that with the Altar Sage defending this side of the river and the Blade of Dawn defending the other, no Nightmare Creature can threaten the livelihoods of humans in this realm. The two of you have lived in peace for centuries, so why would she suddenly attack?\"","Slowly, his expression was twisted with anger.","Putting his cup down, Noctis shook his head.","\"Before that, since when do Transcendent heroes wage war against each other? In this world, we humans are barely holding our own against the Creatures of Corruption! Countless people still suffer from the tyranny of abominable monsters, and our lands are not enough to sustain our numbers! If we want to live, if we want to prosper, we need to push the forces of Corruption back and conquer land. We must fight together, not against each other! So why...\"","His voice gradually grew quiet, and Noctis huffed in dismay.","\"Why are the two of you at each other's throats?\"","The Altar Sage studied Noctis for a few moments, then glanced away and sighed with a wistful smile.","\"You are young, Beast of Twilight. The world you described... it truly did exist, once, when I was young. But everything changes.\"","He glanced at Noctis and smiled.","\"Let me ask you this, Noctis. Do our actions as slayers of monsters have no consequence?\"","As Noctis frowned in confusion, Arelen chuckled and shook his head.","\"It is true that we humans are entangled in a war with the Creatures of Corruption, struggling for dominance over the world. However... after all these centuries, after all these victories, after hundreds of years of the glorious Age of Heroes, how could everything remain the same?\"","He gestured to the musicians playing their instruments and the maidens dancing in front of them.","“When I was young, my city was besieged by terrifying horrors on all sides. Our fields were burned and poisoned every year, and countless men died protecting the walls. I was one of the men defending the walls, as well. Then, I grew more powerful. I grew wiser. I faced those horrors, slaying them one after another — until there was no one left to threaten my city, and its fields sprawled across a vast and prosperous land. The same is true for Irian.\"","Arelen sighed.","“But, Noctis, what do you think happens when we humans have no enemy left to fight? Do we settle down to enjoy peace, forgetting the meaning of violence? Or do we start to look around, noticing what other humans possess, and wishing to own it instead? To be the strongest, the greatest... the most glorious.\"","Shadow tilted his head, listening to the seasoned Transcendent with interest. Human nature was indeed restless, and it was of some interest to the Shadow, so he enjoyed this unexpected insight.","Noctis, however, was not having a good time at all. Instead, the more Arelen spoke, the angrier the young man seemed.","“What are you trying to say, Altar Sage? That the more we heroes slay monsters, the more human blood will be spilled? That once there are no monsters to kill, humans will simply start killing each other? So... the more successful we heroes are, the more horrible human lives will become? And there will never be peace?\"","He scoffed.","“Ha! You are being ridiculous. Preposterous! You have lost sight of what it means to be Transcendent, old man.\"","Arelen studied him for a long while. Eventually, he smiled faintly.","“Of course, there will be peace. In this realm, there will be peace when only one Transcendent rules it. When there is no one left to challenge the ruler’s will, then there'll be peace.\"","He glanced away and added, his voice distant:","“That was how it has been since the dawn of time. Even the mythical First Kingdom only existed for as long as White Abyss ruled over it like a mortal goddess, unreachable and insurmountable, impossible to challenge or depose. Once their sovereign abandoned the people of the First Kingdom, it was quickly torn apart by the ambitions of powerful men.\"","Arelen's expression turned solemn.","\"The world is changing, young Noctis. Slowly but inevitably, it transforms. Humans were weak and few in number before. We struggled to survive in a world full of Corruption — Awakened warriors were rare, and Ascended champions were like a precious treasure. Each Transcendent was like a living legend. But now... how many of us Transcendent heroes are there? How many powerful abominations remain, and how vast a land do they still control?\"","He shook his head.","“Much more than that, now that humanity has accumulated knowledge and gained some strength, Transcendence is not the pinnacle of power anymore. There are already those who defy the heavens to become Supreme... to become sovereigns like those ancient demigods, Kanakht and White Abyss. And hearing of their deeds, which Transcendent doesn't want to attain Supremacy?\"","Noctis glared at him with a dark expression. Eventually, he uttered through gritted teeth:","\"Is Supremacy so important? So desirable? So alluring that those who are meant to protect humans will gather armies and spill human blood instead?\"","The Altar Sage glanced at him with a hint of amusement.","Eventually, he said:","\"Of course, it is.\"","His noble face suddenly seemed older than it was.","\"After all, how can we not desire Supremacy? You are kin to Beast God, Noctis, and even if I am merely a distant descendant, there is a drop of divine blood in my veins as well. We live in a world where gods walk the earth. When looking at the gods, how can we not desire to become gods ourselves?\"","Arelen glanced away with a wistful expression.","“To live for thousands of years instead of hundreds, or even for eternity. To see our people prosper endlessly. To reach for the heavens and bask in their radiance... to conquer them and sit upon a celestial throne. With no common enemy to stand in our way, with no Creatures of Corruption to threaten our lands, who can resist the call of the heavens, the desire to become immortal?\"","Noctis scoffed.","\"Immortality does sound like a lot of fun, but not if it's achieved through despicable means. Surely, Lady Irian is not leading her army to your city because she wishes to live forever.\"","The Altar Sage glanced down.","After a while, he said quietly:","\"True. Supremacy, immortality — those are not insignificant, but they are too distant to be the real cause of this calamity. The real reason for this war, young Noctis... is you.\"","Noctis froze, then raised his eyebrows in disbelief.","\"Me? What are you talking about, old man?! How could I have caused a war between you two?\"","The Altar Sage smiled sadly.","“Did you not slay the Horror of the Viridian Marsh, that Corrupted Tyrant who had haunted the borders of my and Irian's lands for generations? For centuries, both of us tried and failed to kill it. And yet, all those months ago when you visited my city, young hero, you ventured into the marsh and fought a great battle, ending that abomination's profane existence and slaughtering its brood.\"","Noctis frowned.","\"I did, yes! And let me tell you, it was quite a ghastly experience! But so what?\"","Arelen glanced away.","“With the Tyrant gone and its minions either slain or scattered, the miraculously fertile lands near the estuary of the river, as well as precious minerals hidden in the depths of the marsh, were left without a master. Naturally, both Irian and I wanted to lay claim to that land.”","Noctis continued to frown, his expression stormy.","“Couldn't you have split it fairly?\"","The Altar Sage smiled.","“I thought we could. But then, before consulting with me and coming to an agreement, Irian sent settlers to establish a settlement in those newly liberated lands. Because her people needed food.\"","His smile widened a little, becoming somewhat fierce.","“But don't my people need food as well, Beast of Twilight? And those precious minerals, don't my warriors need stronger blades and armor so that they could protect my people, too?\"","His smile dimmed.","Arelen remained silent for a long while, then sighed.","\"So, I ordered my warriors to raze the settlement and slaughter Irian's people. And now, she's coming to exact her vengeance.”","He pursed his lips, a hint of bitterness finding its way into his placid eyes.","“It seems that without the Creatures of Corruption pressing down on us, this vast realm is too small for both Irian and me. One of us must fall.\"","Looking at Noctis, he lingered for a moment. As the music grew quiet and the dancers retreated, the Altar Sage said:","\"Beast of Twilight. Even if it wasn't your intention, the war between Arelen the Altar Sage and Irian, the Blade of Dawn, is happening in part because of what you've done. So, when she arrives... I want you to help me end the war.\"","His words were solemn.","“I want you to help me kill Irian, sunder her army, and bring this land to peace.\""]},{"number":3202,"title":"Chapter 3202 Conflict of Interests","paragraphs":["“That old fool has lost his mind!\"","Having parted with Arelen, Noctis and Shadow had returned to the inn. Noctis had not given the Altar Sage an answer, and the older Transcendent had not insisted on receiving one either — he simply implored the two of them to consider his request. Judging by how angry Noctis was, though, it did not seem like he was inclined to see Arelen's offer in good light.","“Fighting over land? With Lady Irian, of all people?! What was he thinking, ordering his warriors to slaughter her people?!\"","Noctis looked at Shadow, his eyes glinting fiercely.","“And what, the bastard has the gall to blame me for his misdeeds? Asking me to help him kill the Blade of Dawn? Bah! The Altar Sage was supposed to be an icon of wisdom and temperance. Where the hell were his wisdom and temperance when he provoked this war?!\"","The young man cursed quietly, then uttered with a dark expression:","\"If someone has to be killed for this war to stop, shouldn't it be him instead of Lady Irian? He's at fault, so if I were to kill someone, it'd be him!\"","Snuggle, who had climbed out of Shadow's pocket, jumped down to the table and sat down, using an overturned teacup as a chair.","Looking up at the rattled youth, she waved a hand.","\"Calm down.\"","Noctis threw a glare in her direction and scoffed.","\"Whatever do you mean? I'm calm! So calm! I am the calmest person in this realm, no less!\"","Shadow shook his head with a sigh and sat as well.","\"Snuggle is right. You should calm down and think about things clearly. They might not be what they seem to be.\"","Noctis remained silent for a few moments, breathing heavily, then cursed again and pulled back a chair. Crashing down on it, he pierced Shadow with a burning look and asked:","\"How so?\"","Shadow lingered for a bit, then shrugged.","\"The Altar Sage, the Blade of Dawn... you know them better, but neither of them is simple. They are Transcendent rulers with centuries of experience, so do you really think that either one would have acted rashly and recklessly? Would Lady Irian have failed to account for the possibility of Lord Arelen's violent response? Would Arelen have failed to foresee what his actions were certain to cause?\"","Noctis stared at him silently, a hint of confusion finding its way into his gaze. Finally, he grimaced.","“What do you mean?\"","Shadow shook his head.","\"These two are shrewd and seasoned. One doesn't survive long in your line of work without those qualities, definitely not for centuries. So, why do you think Irian claimed the land without even trying to negotiate with Arelen, and why did Arelen — who is supposed to be wise and patient — throw a bloody tantrum and ruthlessly wipe out her settlers?\"","Noctis lingered for a moment or two, then scoffed.","\"How should I know? Greed, ambition? Arelen certainly had a lot to say about his reasons, but I don't buy any of it for a second. He seems to have gone mad!\"","Shadow sighed and shook his head again, then looked at Snuggle.","\"What do you think?\"","Snuggle scratched her head, her small onyx eyes glinting darkly.","Eventually, she said:","“I guess what Arelen said was mostly true. But also a complete lie. It's true that once these lands weren't under threat anymore, with most powerful abominations gone, a conflict between two bordering kingdoms became all but inevitable. But it's a lie that Noctis is the cause — he might have contributed a little, but both Arelen and Irian had to have been contemplating moving against each other for a long time.\"","The little doll lowered her head and added dejectedly:","“All people want to live, after all. And once their lives are not in danger anymore, they always want to live well. But there's never enough nice things for everyone, so someone ends up living better, while others end up looking up at them with envy.\"","Shadow nodded.","“It seems like this war is the result of several unfortunate decisions and miscalculations, Arelen's rash order to slaughter the settlers most of all. But in truth, both he and Irian knew what they were doing. Irian knew that claiming that land without even trying to negotiate would provoke Arelen — she was testing his patience. And Arelen showed her that he had no patience at all, knowing all too well what kind of response that would provoke.\"","He smiled darkly.","“They both got what they wanted. Irian got a true justification to attack and conquer Arelen's city...\"","Noctis frowned.","“Wait, what do you mean the old fool knew what would happen? Even if you are right and the Blade of Dawn was hoping he would give her a reason to invade, what does Arelen get from having her attack his lands?\"","Shadow shrugged.","\"What does he get? Quite a valuable thing, actually. He gets the right to choose the battlefield. After all, Noctis, if you knew that a clash with a powerful adversary was inevitable, would you want to meet them in an open field, or under the walls of your city, which you have been fortifying for centuries?\"","Noctis leaned back, a stunned expression on his face.","He remained silent for a long while, then glanced at Shadow and Snuggle somberly.","\"I guess he is wise, after all. Just... deplorable.\"","A bitter scoff escaped from his lips.","“No wonder that old fool believed he could rope me into his conflict with Lady Irian. He probably thought that a young fool like me would be easy to wrap around his finger... and the worst thing is, he wasn't that wrong.\"","Snuggle giggled.","\"Actually, he probably never hoped to convince you to side with him.\"","Noctis blinked a couple of times.","“What? Then why did he spend so much time trying to convince me?\"","She shook her head and pointed at him with her chubby hand.","\"Think about it, fool! A battle with another Transcendent is only a few days away, and suddenly, another Transcendent arrives in your city — purely by coincidence, he claims. Obviously, Arelen wanted to see if that Irian lady had already recruited you into helping her get rid of him. If you weren't so easy to read and he was left with the smallest hint of doubt back there, he'd probably killed you already — well, perhaps not. Maybe he'd just give you a good beating and lock you up somewhere until this whole war was over. He does seem kind of nice, after all.”","Noctis scoffed.","\"Nice... yes, sure.”","He fell silent, a dark expression on his face. After some time, Noctis laughed and shook his head in dismay.","“I just don't get it! Why? Why do they have to do this? Alright, let's say that there's fertile land and marsh treasures to be had. Do they have to go to war for that? Why can't they just... I don't know... marry and solve their problems in the bedroom! Then, their child would inherit both kingdoms, and everyone can live in peace. The process would be much more enjoyable for all involved parties, needless to say!\"","Hearing that, Snuggle couldn't help but laugh.","Shadow smiled faintly, as well.","He did not say anything immediately, but then shrugged.","\"I think killing each other is both simpler and more straightforward.\"","Noctis gave him a dismayed look.","“Gods, who am I asking? You're a Creature of Shadow! All you shadows ever think about is death.”","Shadow studied him for a moment, then sighed.","“Are you that different?\"","Leaning forward, he picked up the kettle and poured himself some tea.","\"Sure, we shadows are born from death. But don't you heroes spend your entire lives slaughtering Creatures of Corruption? It doesn't matter whether your cause is noble or not. After a lifetime of battles and bloodshed, it's not that surprising that Arelen and Irian grew accustomed to seeing the world through the prism of violence. That is what they know best, after all.\"","He lingered for a moment, then added:","\"I have to give them some credit, though. They could have started a slow, exhausting conflict — one side biting a piece out of the other, the other responding in kind. There would have been endless skirmishes, slow escalation, more and more corpses on both sides. Until, one day, generations later, either Arelen or Irian finally won a significant advantage to wipe the other out.\"","Shadow shook his head.","\"But Arelen didn't want that, so he went for the swiftest solution and ordered Irian's settlement to be entirely destroyed — he wanted this war of theirs to start and end in the span of a single battle. That is something, at least.”","Noctis looked at him darkly.","\"Oh, wow. How noble of him.\"","Finally, he sighed and stood up, walking to the window to take in the vista of the city. After a while, Noctis asked:","“So what am I supposed to do?\"","Shadow raised an eyebrow.","\"What do you want to do?\"","The young man laughed, his voice entirely devoid of joy.","“Would I be asking if I knew the answer?\"","Shadow remained silent for a moment, then shrugged.","\"Well, I'd say you have three options. You can either help Arelen kill Irian, help Irian kill Arelen, or do nothing.”","He scratched the back of his head and then added with a hint of enthusiasm in his voice:","“Actually, there's a fourth option. You can kill both Arelen and Irian. That would be fair for everyone, wouldn't it?\"","Noctis stared at Shadow for a while. Eventually, he turned to look at Snuggle and shook his head.","\"Do me a favor, Snuggle. Remind me never to ask that guy for advice again...\""]},{"number":3203,"title":"Chapter 3203 Ultima Ratio Regum","paragraphs":["In the evening, Noctis was full of dismay and anger.","By the morning, he was in a low and somber mood, savoring tea in the courtyard of the inn with a distant expression on his face. Snuggle was keeping him company, hidden from sight in the draping of his colorful robe — the little doll did not say anything, so Shadow was not sure what her purpose in staying with the youth was.","It was a bit unfamiliar not to feel her tiny weight in his pocket, though... not that he minded.","Surely, he did not mind one bit.","In any case, Shadow had a lot to think about, as well. The conversation with the Altar Sage had stirred his memories, and those memories refused to leave him be. ‘Who doesn't want to be immortal?’ Shadow smiled bitterly.","Among his countless lives, there were some that had been cursed to last forever — even if none did, in the end.","He remembered being a prisoner of the Eternal City, his youthful and flawlessly healthy body infected by the virulent plague of a dead heretic's flesh. Thousands of years of torment, an eternity spent in the darkness of abyssal depths... the pain, the horror, the madness, the collapse of both his spirit and his mind.","He remembered being a Saint whose immortal body became a host for a terrifying vine. That eternity was no less traumatic to recall.","He remembered a shattered skeleton slowly crawling across a sea of obsidian dunes, denied the peaceful embrace of death even after coming uninvited to death's lightless realm.","No matter what kind of immortality Shadow could remember, it was always a curse. And how could it not be?","Death was peace, after all. Death was solace. Those who were refused its grace were doomed to never find either one. Shadow thought about his own endless and unforgiving existence. Wasn't he immortal already? If there was one thing that wielded no power over him, it was time.","However, he was not entirely immune to time, either.","Shadow would not be destroyed by its passage... but he was changing.","He was changing swiftly, in fact.","That was something he had noticed after entering the human city. Ever since meeting Snuggle, and then Noctis... ever since embarking on this misguided journey... he could not quite recognize himself.","Would the Shadow from the past have bothered to hide his identity? To get involved in the tiresome conflict of Transcendent rulers? To explain their schemes to a brash youth, let alone attempt to give that youth advice?","No. The creature Shadow had been would have never come to Arelen’s city, and even if he did, it would not have given that human any time.","But now that Shadow was surrounded by people, exposed to the bright radiance of day, the outer layers of his vast being were dissipating one after another.","What would be revealed when enough of them were gone?","He did not know, and was wary of finding out.","So even if Shadow did not care what would happen to these two Transcendent rulers and their lands, he found himself feeling troubled — no different from Noctis.","It was just that Shadow did not have to do anything, while Noctis had to do a lot.","He had to grow up, come to terms with the nuanced nature of the world, and make a difficult choice — all in the span of several days.","On the first day, Noctis remained in the courtyard of the inn, staring into the distance.","On the second day, he went outside, wandering the streets of the city and looking at the frightened refugees sheltered behind its walls.","On the third day, Noctis wanted to visit the stronghold and confront the Altar Sage... But before he could, war horns bellowed from beyond the city wall, causing a panic among the citizens.","Irian the Blade of Dawn had arrived at the head of her army.","“Damn it! Damn it! Damn it!\"","Cursing loudly, Noctis hurriedly put on his outer robes. He even layered colors that weren't complementary, which revealed just how great the turmoil in his heart was.","Observing him, Shadow raised an eyebrow.","\"So? Did you decide what to do?\"","He was genuinely curious what the youth would choose.","Noctis stared at him for a moment, then cursed under his breath and rushed outside.","\"No!\"","That was a kind of choice, as well. Opening the gates of the inn, Noctis threw a look over his shoulder and added:","\"Let's go take a look first. We can come up with something later.\"","Shadow lingered for a moment, then shrugged and followed. As he did, a squeaky voice resounded from somewhere down below.","“Wait for me! Wait for me!\"","Scurrying across the floorboards, Snuggle jumped clumsily, clutched the hem of his tunic, and climbed up to sit on his shoulder.","There, she huffed while catching her breath — which amused Shadow quite a lot, considering that the little doll did not need to breathe — and pointed forward.","“Let's go! Advance!\"","Shadow sighed.","Feeling like a giant who had been turned into a horse by a tiny human, he caught up with Noctis and pulled him into the shadows. A moment later, the three of them appeared on the battlements atop the wall. Arelen's soldiers were already there, hastily preparing for battle, and the Altar Sage himself had just arrived as well. He stood on the ramparts above the city gates, looking at the plain beyond with a composed expression. Winds tussled his auburn hair, and his eyes glistened in the golden light of dawn.","Out there on the field in front of the city, the enemy army had already assembled its ranks. Irian's warriors were far more numerous than the defenders of the city, and looked more seasoned as well.","As for their commander...","While Arelen had the air of a scholar, Irian the Blade of Dawn looked like a sharp weapon forged to cut down enemies on the battlefield.","She was a radiantly beautiful woman of tall stature, lithe and slender like a drawn sword, wearing armor crafted from white scales and polished bronze. In the rays of the rising sun, the bronze elements of her armor blazed with fiery radiance, as did the head of her long spear.","Dismounting from her snow-white warhorse, Irian raised her head and gazed at the gates of the city. Her hazel eyes were like liquid gold, and her hair was like a waterfall of warm sunlight, gathered into a braid and held in place by a bronze diadem.","“Arelen!\"","Her voice boomed above the vast field, making the soldiers on the wall tremble.","“I've come to seek justice for the lives of the innocent people you slew!\"","Pointing her long spear at the figure of the Altar Sage, Irian gritted her teeth and then shouted:","\"Come down and face me, coward! I'll send them off to the Shadow Realm by spilling your blood!\"","Arelen studied her silently from the battlements, then smiled.","“Innocent people? Those people were thieves who took that which did not belong to them. Surely, you did not bring your army here because I punished some thieves? Oh, but it looks like you did.\"","His smile turned cold and merciless.","“If so, why don't you come up and face me here instead?\"","Irian glared at him for a moment, then laughed darkly.","“So this is how it is. It seems that you have lost all your shame, Arelen the Altar Sage! Fine, then... let us end this dispute with sharp blades instead of treacherous words. Let us show the gods which one of us deserves to be the last one standing!\"","Atop the wall, Noctis clenched his fists.","“These two fools... why are they acting as if lam not even here?\"","Shadow shook his head lightly.","\"Oh, quite the opposite. They are both painfully aware of you. Irian is putting on a brave face, while Arelen is using the fact that you're on this side of the wall to rattle her.\"","A disbelieving chuckle escaped from the young hero's lips.","“Wonderful... simply wonderful. So even by doing nothing, I am still being used to bolster one side.\"","He smiled bitterly and shook his head.","“Ah... when I left the temple, I thought that if I was strong enough, valiant enough, and lucky enough, no enemy would be able to stand in my way. But these few days have taught me a bitter lesson, Shadow. Being strong and brave is great, sure.\"","His smile became a little mocking, as if he was ashamed of himself.","“But being cunning and devious is far more important. Who knew that sages would be deadlier than warriors? Alas, the word is truly mightier than the sword.\"","Shadow gave him a look of confusion.","“Well, of course it is. After all, any decent Shaper can turn a swordsman into a bloodstain by simply opening their mouth.\"","Looking the young Transcendent up and down, he sighed.","“It seems to me that you have chosen the fourth option? You are going to fight Arelen and Irian both?\"","Noctis smiled crookedly.","“What's the point? What will happen if I kill both of them? Nothing good...\"","He remained silent for a moment, then shook his head with a wistful expression.","“I can't do anything to resolve this situation. The best thing I can do... is do nothing.\"","Then, he turned and looked Shadow directly in the eye.","For a moment, a hint of hope flashed in his eyes.","“What about you, Shadow? Can you do something?\"","Sitting on Shadow's shoulder, Snuggle threw a nervous glance at him.","\"No, no... he can't. He promised not to kill anyone!\"","Shadow remained silent, looking at Irian's army with a calm expression.","Could he do something?","And if he could, was there a reason to be involved?","Troubled, Shadow looked down.","Slowly, a strange pain permeated his entire being, forcing him to give Noctis an answer. Finally, he sighed.","\"Can I? I guess I can.\"","On the walls of the city, the archers were nocking arrows on the strings of their bows.","Below the walls, on the field, Irian's army was preparing to charge.","The two Transcendents, former comrades, studied each other somberly. They were ready to clash and kill each other, as well. Mere moments remained until the start of the battle.","But before the first arrow pierced the radiance of dawn...","A dreadful roar suddenly split the heavens apart.","The ground quaked, and a cold wind blew","across the battlefield, causing deathly fear to grasp the hearts of mortal warriors with icy claws.","Something far more terrifying than either of the Transcendent rulers was approaching."]},{"number":3204,"title":"Chapter 3204 Hidden Menace","paragraphs":["The ground shook, and as a terrifying roar thundered above the two armies, dust spilled from between the great stone blocks that formed the wall. Atop the battlements, many of the soldiers lost their balance and fell, dropping their weapons. Below, on the battlefield, the horses of Irian's cavalry buckled in fear, making the riders curse as they struggled to remain in the saddle.","The infantrymen gripped their weapons, looking around with startled and frightened expressions.","Only a few people remained calm and collected, but even their expressions turned grim.","The Altar Sage, the Blade of Dawn, and the Beast of Twilight — the three Transcendent heroes glanced around, momentarily forgetting about their conflict.","\"W—what the hell?\"","Noctis peered into the distance, where a gargantuan hill was slowly crumbling. His voice sounded subdued.","Shadow, meanwhile, was leaning leisurely on the wall of a guard tower, his expression just as calm as it had always been.","He shrugged lightly.","“Who knows?\"","Irian and Arelen, meanwhile, were observing the calamity with wary gazes. Then, briefly, they glanced at each other. Far away, the hill had collapsed entirely, and something gargantuan, hideous, and malevolent moved slowly in the billowing cloud of dust. Suddenly, the radiant light of dawn grew pale and feeble, and the warmth of early summer turned into a piercing chill...","As though death itself had come to reap the two armies.","A moment later, the soldiers paled and staggered, some of them even fainting — that was because the overwhelming presence of the hidden menace washed over them, followed by the suffocating pressure of a vast and alien Will.","Sitting on Shadow's shoulder, Snuggle turned her head to look at him, then stood up slowly and pulled on his hair.","Her squeaky voice was reduced to a barely audible whisper:","“H—hey! Are you not... overdoing it a little?\"","Shadow just smiled faintly.","“Am I? It depends on how strong these mortal heroes are, I suppose.\"","He spoke quietly enough for Noctis not to hear — the young Transcendent was not listening to Shadow, anyway, his entire attention focused on the immense figure moving slowly under the veil of dust. Finally, the Altar Sage uttered a Verse, and a powerful gale tore apart the cloud of dust, revealing the true form of the unknown creature.","Standing atop the wall, he was the first to behold it. His face paled, and his gaze turned grim.","Out there on the plain in front of the city, a towering abomination was slowly crawling out of the shattered earth. Its body was long and segmented, like that of a centipede, but its head resembled a giant human skull that was missing the lower jaw, with three empty eye sockets that hid impenetrable darkness.","The chitinous carapace of the giant abomination was so black that it seemed to absorb the surrounding light. The enormous skull, however, was vibrantly scarlet, as if it had been bathed in an ocean of human blood until the surface of the ancient bone fully absorbed it.","Finally climbing from the depths of earth, the hideous centipede raised its long neck. Even with most of its body still on the ground, the scarlet skull loomed at least a hundred meters above it, turned in the direction of the city.","The three empty eye sockets of the titanic abomination stared at the three Transcendent heroes, eerily emotionless, the unfathomable pools of darkness hidden within them still and hollow.","What was not still, however, were hundreds of ghastly maws that revealed themselves on the inner side of the creature's belly, gnashing myriads of teeth as they revealed the crimson flesh of the monster. Witnessing the great immensity of the abhorrent creature, the soldiers of Irian's army, who stood between the city and the subterranean horror, took an unconscious step back — in the direction of the wall they had been meant to besiege.","Irian herself seemed rattled, as well. Looking at the eerie scarlet skull, she gripped her spear and whispered in a stunned voice:","\"A Great Monster!\"","She could not see the soul of the giant creature, of course. But merely by sensing the oppressive power of its presence, as well as the malevolent flavor of its Will, she could make a judgment.","Atop the wall, Arelen wore a grave expression, as well.","Noctis, meanwhile...","Seemed thoroughly appalled.","“A centipede! Ah, eww! Why did it have to be a damn centipede?! I hate them!\"","He shuddered, grimacing in utter disgust. Shadow spared him an amused look.","“That's what you worried about?\"","He was a little bit hurt.","After all, he had gone into a lot of trouble to create that monster.","The giant Nightmare Creature was not an Nightmare Creature at all. Instead, it was merely a construct woven out of manifested shadows, controlled by his will. Its flesh was equal in toughness to that of a Supreme being, since it was infused with his Supreme essence.","As for the power of its presence and the malevolence of its Will, those were simply the presence and Will of Shadow — a sliver of them, at least — which he revealed when the monster appeared.","Creating such a monstrosity was no easy feat, but not that difficult either. Its carapace, its muscles, its tendons, its fangs, and all the other parts of its enormous body — Shadow manifested them all and then connected them together into a functional organism, breathing a false spark of life into that organism with his nuanced control.","He had even gone into the trouble of changing the color of its bones and its flesh, thinking that showing a creature painted entirely black would put Noctis into a difficult position. The youth had just returned from supposedly vanquishing an unknown horror that dwelled in eternal darkness, after all, so Shadow didn't want anyone to think that the monster followed the Beast of Twilight to this peaceful city from a distant realm.","As for whether Irian and Arelen would believe that the giant centipede was indeed a Creature of Corruption... Shadow did not particularly care. Unlike soul essence, his own was the essence of shadows — so, even if they had means of peering into the souls of living beings, they would not see the familiar silver radiance.","And even if they discerned that something was not quite right, it did not matter. The nature of the monster was not as important as its perceived malice and intent to destroy the city.","\"Irian!\"","Standing atop the wall, Arelen shouted his adversary's name. The radiant Transcendent who had come to kill him glanced up, and the two seemed to converse silently, their gazes full of concerned wariness.","Then, after exchanging a nod, they both rushed toward the towering creature side by side.","Noctis cursed and leaped down from the wall, as well, dashing to follow them. Moments later, Shadow and Snuggle were left alone among terrified soldiers.","\"What the hell did you create, Shadow?\"","Snuggle's voice sounded oddly weak. Looking down at her in surprise, Shadow raised an eyebrow.","“What? It's merely a construct.\"","He paused for a moment, then added with a shrug:","“Actually, I didn't even have to work that hard on it. That thing was already something I had considered creating — back when I was thinking of making a better vessel for you. A battle golem, of sorts.\"","The little doll trembled and stared at him in dismay.","“T—that? You wanted me — me! — to climb inside that thing? That disgusting, ghastly thing over there?!\"","Shadow looked at her in confusion.","“Why? Look at it. It's very sturdy, can move below and above ground really fast, and has a lot of ways to kill enemies. And it is very menacing — instilling the adversary with fear is half the victory, you know.\"","He scratched the tip of his nose awkwardly.","“Admittedly, it can't fly. Adding a sufficient number of wings introduced too many points of vulnerability to the carapace, so I was left with no choice but to scrap that idea. Still. I think it turned out pretty well.\"","He smiled proudly.","\"I call it... the Giant Red Skull Centipede, Prototype One.\"","Snuggle groaned and covered her face with a hand.","“Prototype One, he says... gods have mercy, look how proud he is! He's completely serious, too!\"","Shadow blinked a couple of times.","\"It's a fitting name, though? I don't see the issue.\"","Perhaps Snuggle was simply too young to appreciate his stellar namingship.","Well... what else would one expect from a doll called Snuggle?","Far in the distance, the giant monster lowered its head and flowed forward like a river of scarlet darkness, moving toward the three Transcendent heroes with terrifying speed, the ground turning into a shredded mess of torn soil and seething mucus wherever it passed.","Shadow sighed.","‘All that work, only for it to be destroyed...’","Even though he had promised Snuggle not to kill anyone and created this construct specifically to be slain by the mortal heroes... he still found himself secretly rooting for the giant centipede.","After all, if its own creator couldn't support this soulless construct, wouldn't it be just too pitiful?","A split second later, on the plain in front of the city, three Transcendent heroes — Arelen the Altar Sage, Irian the Blade of Dawn, and Noctis, the Crimson Beast of Twilight — clashed with the harrowing Nightmare Creature... Giant Red Skull Centipede, Prototype One.","Their battle would become a legend all across the mortal realms in the future, one day soon."]},{"number":3205,"title":"Chapter 3205 Three Heroes Faced a Dreadful Worm","paragraphs":["\"No, no! You are telling it wrong, blind fool! You weren't even there, so what do you know? But I! I saw it all! I was standing atop the wall when the three heroes faced the dreadful beast of the Underworld, the ghastly spawn of appalling Corruption, the great and grotesque Nightmare Creature, devourer of human souls... the Giant Red Skull Centipede!\"","The streets of the city were lively today.","In the early morning, when Shadow and Noctis stopped to enjoy one last cup of tea before leaving the city to resume their journey, they had no choice but to hear people retelling the story of the recent battle.","Despite being praised as a valiant hero, Noctis wore a sullen expression. Cursing quietly, he threw a resentful glance at Shadow, then raised his cup and used the wide sleeves of his colorful robe to hide his face.","Shadow smiled faintly.","The soldier, meanwhile, continued his story.","\"Hear, hear! There I was, standing atop the wall and drawing the string of my bow when the ground shook, and a ghostly chill permeated the air. The soldiers of Lady Irian's army below the wall all scattered and fell, their horses foaming at the mouth and going mad from terror. At that moment, all of us felt the icy breath of Death, and our limbs grew weak and feeble. Only three courageous heroes endured it — our wise ruler, Arelen the Altar Sage, the brave and radiant Lady Irian, the Blade of Dawn, and young Noctis, Child of the Moon... the Beast of Twilight!\"","Shadow looked at Noctis and said in a low tone:","“Did you hear? He's talking about you, Child of the Moon!\"","Noctis lowered his head and groaned.","“What was that? I didn't hear anything!\"","Shadow chuckled.","The soldier slammed his cup, sending drops of tea flying into the air, and glanced around with wide eyes.","\"And there, in the distance, was the Great Creature of Corruption — the ancient horror who crawls below the world, the corpse eater, the guardian of the Abyss. The Giant Red Skull Centipede! Surely, you must have heard of the infamous calamities it had caused throughout the ages!\"","A few of the listeners nodded hesitantly, their faces pale.","“Right... right. Giant Red Skull Centipede? Of course, I heard of it! I am not some ignorant fool, after all. Isn't it... uh... isn't it that thing Heart God once cast into the abyss after it gnawed on the insides of the Heart Tree's fruit?\"","“No, you're thinking of the Spirit Worm, Abundance! The Giant Red Skull Centipede is a different worm; it's the corpse worm that devoured the flesh of Beast God's first avatar!\"","“That's right! Not only that, but I also heard that it was the bane of First Humans. White Abyss herself had once battled the Giant Red Skull Centipede, but the creature's profane carapace could not be burned even by her flames!\"","“Goodness... such a terrifying Nightmare Creature...\"","\"To think that it actually burrowed under our city. Gods, I am still trembling!\"","The soldier glanced at his listeners with scorn.","\"Indeed! That is how dreadful that Nightmare Creature was. I saw it with my own two eyes — as long as a mountain chain, its head reaching the heavens... no, not simply reaching the heavens! It was so enormous that clouds were like its crown, surrounding the scarlet skull and spilling out of its terrifying eye sockets. It had a myriad of bloody maws! Ten myriads of dreadful legs! When it moved, it was as if the rivers of the Underworld spilled from the depths of earth, consuming the world like a tide of darkness!\"","He took a deep breath.","“All of us were ready to leave for the Shadow Realm... except for the three heroes. Undaunted by the ghastly visage of the ancient curse, they rushed across the plain to meet it. Ah, the sight of them! The majesty of the Altar Sage, the breathtaking radiance of the Blade of Dawn, the thoughtless brashness of the Beast of Twilight...\"","Noctis turned his head and hissed through gritted teeth.","“Did he just call me a thoughtless bastard?!\"","Shadow gestured for him to calm down.","“He did not. And keep your voice down.\"","They were sitting in a corner, far from the gathered crowd. However, drawing attention would still be troublesome.","From Shadow's pocket, Snuggle squeaked quietly:","\"Even if he did, so what?!\"","Noctis hid his face, while the soldier continued:","“When the three heroes clashed with the monstrous Nightmare Creature... the sky quaked! The ground shattered! The winds screamed in agony, and the fierce thunder of that terrifying clash echoed across all mortal realms, reaching even the blessed reaches of the six Divine abodes. Lady Irian struck first, her spear shining like a ray of sunlight... but, alas! Oh, woe! The creature's carapace, forged from adamantine darkness, was too tough to be pierced! With not even a scratch left on it...\"","The tale continued in the same manner.","“And that was when our wise lord assumed his Transcendent form, his wings reaching toward the heavens. His talons sank into the cracks between the plates of the Nightmare Creature’s armor, and his beak fell upon the scarlet skull as a hammer falls on an anvil, like an owl snatching a snake from tall grass...\"","\"The Nightmare Creature bellowed then, its voice scattering all hope! Not even valiant Lady Irian could withstand the ghastly power of that call, falling to one knee and spitting a mouthful of blood. Each drop was like a precious ruby, and her porcelain face turned to pure alabaster, making it even more tantalizing...\"","“And it was then! When all hope seemed to be lost! That the Crimson Beast of Twilight rushed forward like a torrent of pale moonlight, like a ghostly wolf woven out of bravery and bloodlust, his vicious fangs sinking into the black carapace of the ancient horror. He tore at the creature with his claws, shredding its neck in his jaws, completely fearless!\"","Eventually, the soldier ran out of breath. As his listeners leaned forward, he gulped down his tea and let out a long sigh.","“And that was how the three mortal heroes slew a monster as old as the gods themselves! The Altar Sage held its skull in place, the Beast of Twilight tore apart its neck, and the Blade of Dawn delivered the decisive blow, severing the skull from the Nightmare Creature’s endless body. The Giant Red Skull Centipede writhed then, hills and forests perishing in the violence of its death throes. By luck, the warriors of Lady Irian's army had retreated to the city wall by then — if not, all of them would have perished, as well.\"","He shuddered.","\"And once the Nightmare Creature lost its life, its body turned into a tide of darkness, flowing back into the depths of earth — not even the ghastly skull remained. All that remained were two enormous soul shards. Our lord took one, while Lady Irian took the other — young Noctis, meanwhile, being a humble and modest youth, simply bowed to his elders, saying that protecting humans from the horrors of Corruption was already a worthy reward.\"","A lone tear rolled down the soldier's weathered face.","“Such virtue!\"","The soldier's tale was quite engaging. In fact, similar stories were being told all around the city at the moment — wandering rhapsodes were already writing songs about the battle, each competing in who could exaggerate it more.","Noctis, however, gnashed his teeth.","\"Says who?! I wanted a soul shard, too! They just snatched them first!\"","Shadow glanced at him and raised an eyebrow.","“You want one? There's plenty more where those two came from. I can donate a couple more.\"","The soul shards had come from the depths of his soul, where he had stored them centuries ago. All kinds of creatures had visited his kingdom over the ages, and after killing them, Shadow had little use for their soul shards — so he had quite a few by now. Noctis stared at him for a moment, then shook his head.","\"You took all the fun out of it, so what's the point?\"","The soldier was still talking, but there was no point in listening anymore — not that there had been.","In truth, the three Transcendents had barely managed to destroy the Giant Red Skull Centipeded, Prototype One. Shadow had even considered giving in a little, but luckily, Noctis stepped up at that moment and helped them bring the construct down. All three heroes were severely wounded during the battle, though, having barely survived — that was fortunate, at least. After dealing with the Great Monster, Arelen and Irian were in no mood to fight each other. So, in a peculiar turn of events, the besieging army ended up camping under the city wall, with some soldiers even entering the city to purchase supplies and receive medical attention.","The war was over... for now, at least.","Noctis sighed.","“You could have warned me, you know! I was so proud of myself... until Snuggle informed me that the supposed Great Monster was not a Creature of Corruption at all, and instead a puppet you created out of boredom.\"","He shivered and gave Shadow an uneasy look.","“By the way, Shadow... forgive me for saying this. But you're a sick bastard. That thing you made was so abhorrent! What kind of troubled mind can even come up with something like this?!\"","Shadow contemplated the answer for a moment.","“I'm pretty healthy, I think?\"","Noctis let out a disbelieving laugh, then shook his head and shivered once more.","“By the moon... if this is what he makes when he's bored, I'm scared to imagine what he'll do if something actually angers him.\"","He remained silent for a short while, then asked.","\"I still don't get it, though. After the battle, both Irian and Arelen were severely weakened. Wasn't it a perfect moment to stab each other in the back? But they suddenly seem nice and friendly again. In fact, it's like nothing happened — as if they weren't at each other's throats just a few days ago.\"","Shadow shrugged.","\"That's to be expected. You really don't understand why? It's very simple.\"","He poured himself more tea.","“Ambition, aspiration... powerlust, greed... loyalty to one's subject and the desire to leave your mark upon the world, to conquer the heavens. All of those are powerful motivations, but there is one thing that trumps them all. Do you know what it is?\"","Noctis slowly shook his head.","In response, Shadow just smiled faintly.","“It's fear. Irian and Arelen have forgotten fear, but I reminded them. I showed them that, in this world, there is no safety. There is no assurance. Even if you spend your entire life cleansing your lands of abominations, one day, a horror that you cannot defeat alone can just pop up from underground and swallow your city whole.\"","He sighed and then added, feeling a strange melancholy:","“After all, no one survives in this world alone.”","Shadow chuckled.","\"So, in a sense... even if all else fails to bring peace, fear can.\"","Noctis stared at him silently for a while, then asked in a subdued tone:","“So you think that there will really be peace in this land now?\"","Shadow lingered a little, then slowly shook his head.","\"There will be... for a while. But in the end, war will come to replace it again.\"","He finished his tea and rose, ready to leave the tavern — and the city — behind him.","“In the end, Arelen was right. This land will only know true peace when there's only one power left to rule it.”","With that, he turned around and headed away.","Noctis grimaced, then followed him.","\"I think you're wrong, though.\"","He smiled.","“There are six gods, after all, and they don't often quarrel. There are even other deities —a throng of Spirits, even the daemons. And the heavens are not consumed by war, are they?\"","The Shadow glanced ahead, his expression a little wistful.","\"Yeah. The heavens are at peace.\"","They were, for now.","Soon, the three of them left through the open gates of the city, passed the encampment of Irian's army, and headed away.","The city slowly disappeared from view. The road ahead was long.","Their journey was only just beginning, after all..."]},{"number":3206,"title":"Chapter 3206 Bad Weather","paragraphs":["People had always imagined hell as a place full of fire. But, as it turned out, hell was full of wind and water instead.","NQSC was swallowed by a storm. The sky was obscured by a dark, menacing veil of clouds, and hurricane winds howled as they tore through the crumbled remains of the city barriers and collapsed buildings in the outer rings of the city. Rain fell like a wall, flying sideways from the sheer force of the powerful gale. Flashes of lightning burned the darkness away, and deafening claps of thunder roared high above, as if there was a malevolent, hungry dragon hidden in the storm.","Storms like this one had been happening more and more often over the past four years, eventually fusing into a never-ending deluge of calamity.","Of course, despite all the damage caused by the unceasing natural catastrophes, it was merely a background for the true disaster.","The true disaster was the Nightmare Gates that now surrounded the city like siege towers and the endless swarms of abominations escaping them each day.","The world was truly and utterly ending.","In fact, it was already halfway gone.","It had started slowly, but then proceeded swiftly. There were simply more and more Nightmare Gates, more abominations, and more casualties among the soldiers who desperately protected Earth from being torn apart. Then, pieces of the waking world began fusing with the Dream Realm, adding their weight to its patchwork surface.","Once the two realms became partially fused, the Nightmare Creatures did not need Gates to travel between them anymore. That alone added immense pressure to the strained defenses of humanity, but there was even more damage. A planet was a closed and finely tuned system, after all. Once a hostile mystical realm started taking bites out of it, nature itself went insane, causing rapid and unpredictable changes.","Hence, the storms.","Here in NQSC, at least, it was mainly storms. Elsewhere, it was something else — volcanic eruptions, earthquakes, tsunamis, sharp temperature changes...","It was not all bad, though. Yes, the infusion of alien air had caused the sky above NQSC to go insane... but it was clean air. Even now that the air filtration barriers were breached or collapsed, people were not being poisoned on the street — in fact, they could breathe freely without face masks for the first time in hundreds of years.","Even the end of the world had its perks.","“Move aside, bastards! Let them through! As soon as the rear vehicle clears, close ranks!\"","“What are you doing, fool?! This guy is still alive! Drag him back and hand him over to the medics!\"","“Report! Left highrise turrets, ammunition spent!\"","“Sir! They're coming!\"","“Argh, curse it all! Anyone whose armor still has more than thirty percent charge left, advance to the front row!\"","“Best seats in the establishment! Let's enjoy the show, gentlemen!\"","“Light them up!\"","On a street between two battered dormitory towers, the joints of powered armor suits hissed as soldiers unleashed a hail of bullets and explosive rounds into the rushing tide of Nightmare Creatures. Behind them, towering MWPs charged their mass drivers, rising monstrous machine guns to bathe the abominations in lead and tungsten hail. The turrets above the highrises spun, spitting out long streams of tracer rounds.","The roaring salvo of countless shots drowned out the deafening blast of thunder... but it failed to drown out the chilling wails of the rushing Nightmare Creatures.","The soldiers of the first line of defense paled, preparing to deploy their bayonets.","\"I... I don't think I like this show, guys!\"","“Wow, really?! You don't say!\"","“It's about to end, though! At least for us!\"","\"What a silver lining!\"","The soldiers had been fighting the entire day, slowly retreating street by street as the civilians of the breached district were being evacuated deeper into the city. Now, however, it looked like for many of the soldiers, this was going to be the last stand.","Just before the tide of abominations overwhelmed the makeshift defensive position, a swift figure streaked through the air and plummeted into their mass.","“Brace for impact!\"","There was a muffled boom.","In the next moment, the entire center of the Nightmare Creature horde was pulverized, hundreds of them dying in an instant. It was difficult to see because of the torrential rain and furious wind, but countless abominations that were close to the figure simply turned into bloody mist, while those that had been further away were merely torn to tiny pieces.","Hide, chitin, flesh, bone — everything was crushed and ground to dust in a split second, as if struck by a celestial hammer, flung outward by a heavy shockwave.","A heartbeat later, lightning illuminated the world, and the startled soldiers saw a blurry streak moving through the swarm of Nightmare Creatures with astonishing speed. Wherever it passed, scores of abominations were severed, beheaded, and split open — as if the binds that held their bodies together were being undone.","One soldier, whose visual acuity was better than most, caught a glimpse of a great zweihander flashing in a magnificent arc.","\"It's... it's the Lady of Sorrow!\"","\"What?! Isn't she a Saint?!\"","“Since when is Lady Sorrow in NQSC?!\"","“A Saint has descended from the sky... now that's an ending!\"","“Stop staring and push forward, fools! Support the lady and her people!\"","“Left highrise turrets have finished the reloading sequence!\"","“The last convoy has entered the Barrier, sir!\"","\"Advance!\"","The situation on this battlefield had changed in an instant. Lady of Sorrow — Tamar of Clan Sorrow — was one of the youngest Saints of humanity, having conquered her Third Nightmare only recently. However, her fame had been steadily spreading among people even before that, when she was a mere Master. Most of the renowned figures of humanity were affiliated with one of the great powers in one way or another. There were Saints serving one of the two queens, Morgan of Valor or Song Seishan, and those who served Nightwalker and the House of Night. There were some who followed Ananke of Weave or one of the three Supreme protectors of the waking world.","Tamar of Sorrow and her small band of elite warriors, however, were one of the few independent forces that roamed the realms while serving no one. Nobody ever knew where they would pop up, which battlefield she would grace with her presence... wherever it was, however, countless Nightmare Creatures died, and tides of battle were usually reversed.","Invigorated, the soldiers pushed forward, aiming to eliminate the remaining abominations before organizing an orderly retreat.","Tamar, meanwhile, cleaved far into the crumbling horde, moving deeper and deeper like a whirlwind of blood and steel.","[Don't get too excited. Pull back.]","The voice came from a Memory used by members of the Shadow Clan — with this many Gates, technology became more and more unreliable, causing a crisis of command and communication among the soldiers of humanity. Where technology failed, sorcery and Awakened picked up the slack.","In that regard, the Shadow Clan was better off than any other faction.","Tamar smiled grimly.","[Who says that I am excited?]","Finally, she reached the Tyrant who controlled the horde from the rear. Leaping into the air, she stepped on it to change her trajectory and avoid a deadly blow, then did it again to launch herself toward the creature's massive head.","[I am exhausted. I want to lie down. I want to take a hot shower. I want to eat something warm, too...]","The creature's head split apart, a fountain of fetid blood mixing with the falling rain. Tamar landed on the wet asphalt, slid a few dozen meters, and brought herself to a halt by transforming her momentum into a blast of concussive force that tore a hole in the nearest abomination.","[Most of all, I want to get somewhere dry. Damn rain...]","Her Memory spoke again:","[Hey. That was uncalled for.]","In that moment, a powerful gust of wind slammed into Tamar, obscuring her vision with a veil of water.","Half-blinded, she looked around.","‘It is time to pull back, indeed.'","She had performed well in front of the soldiers, but in truth, she was not in good shape. Beneath the armor, her body was bruised and battered, littered with wounds — and beneath them, there were the wounds from the previous battlefield that had been treated, but had not healed fully yet.","Things had been getting worse and worse as of late, and there was no respite in sight. Antarctica had fallen first. By now, it was most likely fully absorbed by the Dream Realm, most of it transported to somewhere beyond the Burned Forest. As such, it had become an open wound in the flesh of Earth, unleashing an endless flood of Nightmare Creatures — that alone would have been enough to overwhelm the remaining Quadrants... if not for Revel and the Shadow Clan.","Somewhere out there, on the unknown northern front of apocalypse, Saint Revel was leading the forces of the Shadow Clan, including the powerful Shadows and the legion of shades their boss had left in her care, against the Barrow Wraiths and countless abominations of the Burned Forest. In fact, she had staged a counteroffensive and invaded the charred Death Zone a couple of years ago.","Because of Revel pulling the attention of all those Nightmare Creatures to the Forgotten Shore, fewer of them were spilling into the waking world.","Still... their number was enough to make the oceans of Earth completely inaccessible. Navigating them had always been perilous, but now, it was pure suicide. Even Saints did not dare to traverse the oceans.","The colonies in South America had been evacuated, but the three remaining Quadrants were completely isolated from each other now. With global infrastructure in tatters, famine had long become a real possibility — even with most population centers possessing robust food self-sustenance systems, those had long been cripplied by the spreading influence of the Call.","In the end, the only thing that was preventing humanity from starving was the Night Garden and its captain, who could both carry people from the waking world to the Dream Realm and bring food from the Dream Realm to the waking world on the way back. Raised by Wolves could help, as well.","It was quite ironic... before, people of the Dream Realm staved off starvation with supplies from Earth, But now, the situation was entirely reversed.","Which was not to say that the people in the Dream Realm knew no hunger. The more the situation in the waking world worsened, the more refugees poured into the human enclaves there. By now, a good one-third of humanity had left its cradle, pushing the population of the Dream Realm well beyond one billion.","And the Dream Realm... the Dream Realm was in no way ready to accept this many people.","Things weren't going well there either, after all.","On Earth, the three remaining Quadrants were under a constant siege, both from beyond and from within. In the Dream Realm, meanwhile, the same was true for the three Domains — even with the Sovereigns leading the battle, humanity was struggling to hold on to its land.","Expanding their reach, of course, had become completely impossible.","The wilderness was too dangerous, and the Citadel Cities weren't made of rubber. By now, every single one of them was overpopulated and suffering from resource shortages.","A few had already been lost.","'We are not dead yet.'","Tamar looked at the ravaged urban landscape in front of her with a grim expression.","They were not dead... but they were certainly dying.","Humanity was like a wounded soldier slowly bleeding out on the ground, hoping that a medic would arrive in time to save them.","It was only that the medics who could save humanity were stuck in a Nightmare.","They had been gone for four years already, and nobody knew when they would come back."]},{"number":3207,"title":"Chapter 3207 The Apocalypse Happened Yesterday","paragraphs":["As Tamar retreated, nimbly dashing through the air when towering carcasses blocked her way, the remains of the horde tried to pursue her. Whenever a Nightmare Creature got too close, a black arrow fell from above, its passage almost invisible in the stormy darkness. The arrows struck the abominations unerringly, pinning them down — however, not a single creature died.","Thinking that Rain was enduring the storm somewhere on the roof made Tamar feel better. After all, there was nothing more sad than being miserable alone... being miserable together with a friend was much better.","‘Damn storm...’","The battle for NQSC had been long and gruelling, but for Tamar, the constant rain and unceasing wind felt more exhausting than endless waves of Nightmare Creatures — which was a bit peculiar, considering that her ancestral Citadel used to stand atop the Weeping Goddess.","Until the King of Nothing destroyed it.","Who would have guessed that she'd be praying for his return one day?","His and that of her boss, of course, as well as the other two Supremes who had challenged the Fifth Nightmare.","[I'm retreating.]","The soldiers almost reached the Barrier. Their retreat was orderly, but just to be safe, the Shadow Clan agents under Tamar's command were covering it. Now, it was time for them to escape as well.","‘How many hours can we rest?'","Revel was in the Dream Realm, tied in a vicious war against the Barrow Wraiths and the horrors of the Burned Forest... for now. Last Tamar heard, something was stirring in the rotten corpse of the dead World Tree — so it was unclear how long the Lightslayer would be able to hold on.","That battlefield was too deadly for most human members of the Shadow Clan, though. So, most of them had been sent to various flashpoints of the apocalypse both in the Dream Realm and on Earth, moving in the shadows and accomplishing tasks that demanded an elite force with a delicate touch.","That was how it had been in the beginning, at least... by now, many of them operated in the open, pretending to be independent Awakened — those who were still alive, of course. Tamar had conquered her Third Nightmare recently and was hurriedly sent to the Northern Quadrant, where Rain was in command.","Despite still being a Master, the Princess of Shadows had become somewhat irreplaceable for their ragtag group of knaves and misfits. Her powers were simply too mystical, while her ability as a sorceress was second to none. So, no one was surprised that she was in charge of Saints despite being of a lower Rank, still.","By now, many of humanity's forces had been pulled to NQSC... but even with all of them fighting desperately to keep the city intact, the Nightmare Creatures were slowly pushing them back.","The outskirts had been swallowed almost a year ago. The outer barriers held out for many months, but were eventually breached and conquered by abominations. Now, the last district in the outer ring of the city was being abandoned... which meant that the defenders were fully retreating behind the Barrier.","The Barrier was something that Nightwalker had created. It was a zone surrounding the inner city where space was so torn and twisted that it had become a demented, deadly labyrinth — if one didn't have a special enchanted token, they could very well become lost there for the rest of their lives.","Or for eternity.","Nightmare Creatures still made their way through, but many of them perished or were weakened in the process. So, while the Barrier was not a panacea, it helped the defenders of the city keep at least the inner districts intact.","The battle for NQSC was tough...","But then again, it was tough everywhere. The entire population of the Eastern Quadrant was locked in a bloody war against the horrors that crawled onto the coast from the depths of the ocean. The Western Quadrant was already being consumed by the Dream Realm, and the situation there was even more desperate than here in the north.","Granted, there were relatively few people left there who had not been evacuated to the Dream Realm already — the Northern Quadrant was slowly and surely becoming the last bastion of humanity on Earth, as well as its final battlefield.","Out there in the Dream Realm, the situation was not much better. Its territory was shifting, new regions appearing in the middle of well-charted lands. As a result, old horrors that had been resting in their lairs for eons were stirring, directing their gazes at the human settlements.","The Stormsea was boiling and seething, rivers of blood flowing into its misty water. Silver Web was still holding, and the city in the delta of the River of Tears was holding as well — but they were under constant siege. The basin of the great river had become one vast battlefield, with isolated Citadel Cities barely holding the Nightmare Creatures at bay.","In the east, the eerie darkness had finally stopped spreading after swallowing half a dozen Citadels. However, nobody knew when it would start moving again. Ravenheart was being besieged by the snow wraiths of the frozen wastelands. Bastion was faring relatively well, but the connection to the northern territories had been cut...","And recently, waves of powerful Nightmare Creatures had begun to flow out from the belt of Death Zones lying between the Godgrave and the Stormsea. Morgan and her warriors took the brunt of that tide of horrors, even if some of it spilled into the basin of the River of Tears as well.","Morgan, Seishan, and Ananke... each of them had battled Cursed Nightmare Creatures in the past four years. For now, they were yet to be defeated, but each of those battles had left scars both on their bodies and on the surface of the Dream Realm itself.","The wardens of the waking world had fared somewhat better, but they were exhausted by the need to both fight endlessly and resist the hostile pressure of the very realm they were trying to protect. Still, their presence was like a ray of hope in the sea of nightmares — every time the soldiers of humanity witnessed Raised By Wolves, Nightingale, or Soul Reaper, their morale soared.","It was just that only one of them could be present in the waking world at a time — they had to take turns entering the battlefield, lest a dire crisis happened when none of them could return. And there were too many battlefields on Earth for one being to be enough, even if that being was Supreme.","\"Ready your tokens!\"","Tamar was the last to arrive in front of the Barrier, rushing ahead of the pursuing mob of Nightmare Creatures. Several cohorts of the Shadow Clan fighters were already waiting for her there, clad in sleek suits of black armor, armed with both Memories and mundane weapons. Rain had descended from the highrise as well, looking at the turrets the soldiers had to abandon with regret.","Tamar leaned on her zweihander, breathing heavily. All around her, her soldiers pulled the enchanted markers that would allow them to pass the Barrier from beneath their armor.","At that moment, blaring alarms roared all across the city.","Looking at her mechanical watch — a relic that had become priceless ever since humanity began to settle the Dream Realm while the Call began disrupting delicate electronics — she cursed.","‘Moonrise...’","Many terrifying things had happened when the boundary between the waking world and the Dream Realm began to become blurry, but none was more terrifying than what was happening to the Moon.","There had been a saying before that looking at the Moon too closely was perilous. Now, however, it was especially so — somewhere along the way, simply glancing up while the moon was visible in the sky became deadly. Many people had died, many had instantly gone mad, and even more of them had immediately become infected by Corruption.","Those who were mundane were dragged into the First Nightmare, most of them turning into abominations and slaughtering everyone around them. Those who were Awakened simply turned, to a much more devastating effect.","And with every month, the influence of the Moon was only growing more intense, frightening, and malevolent.","Tamar was a Saint, and the sky above NQSC was obscured by heavy clouds. Still, she lowered her gaze.","At that moment, another flash of lightning illuminated the word, and Rain pulled back the hood of her black raincoat to look up. Her expression did not seem good. Knowing that her friend often sensed things that other people couldn't, Tamar tensed.","\"What?\"","Rain hesitated for a moment, then gritted her teeth and pointed at the sky. Tamar hesitated, then glanced at the seething mass of storm clouds above them.","There, hidden by the hurricane, something gargantuan was moving between the bolts of lightning. In fact, it seemed as if the heavens had gone mad, attacking the titanic form in berserk fury. Dozens, then hundreds of twisting eclectic arcs struck the colossal shadow as it slowly revealed itself.","The brilliance of myriad bolts of lightning illuminated the world like a pale sun.","Tamar paled.","A moment later, the Night Garden revealed itself from the storm.","The great ship had descended below the stormclouds, revealing its battered form to the people sheltered in the city. Its size was so immense that it was difficult to fathom, wreathed in lightning and glowing with residual energy.","And, at the moment, another form — one infinitely vast, grotesque, and repulsive — was wrapped around the ship's hull, straining to crush it.","Tamar couldn't see the upper part of the giant Nightmare Creature, but each of its tattered wings was large enough to cover an entire district of the city. One was severed and charred; the other was clawing at the Mainmast Pagoda of the living ship with giant, curving talons.","Myriad arrows streaked from the deck of the Night Garden to pierce its body, and enormous cannons roared one after another, each taking out huge chunks of flesh from its belly. An enormous figure woven out of starlight was rending the creature's back... but even with all these efforts, it didn't seem to be on the threshold of death yet.","Tamar took an involuntary step back.","\"What... what the hell is this?\"","A Titan? A Cursed Nightmare Creature?","\"We need to get behind the Barrier.\"","Rain's voice sounded calm, but Tamar knew her well enough to recognize an underlying layer of trepidation.","She glanced at her friend with a silent question.","Rain pulled the barrier token out and turned back.","\"It's falling. It's going to impact somewhere beyond the city... but close. So, we need to run. What are you standing around for, guys?! Run, run, run!\"","Throwing one last look at the Night Garden, Tamar gritted her teeth and dove into the Barrier.","Behind her, Nightmare Creatures were flooding the ravaged street like a grotesque river.","A bolt of lightning flashed, and a deafening thunderclap shook the world.","Another day of the apocalypse was coming to an end."]},{"number":3208,"title":"Chapter 3208 Out of the Frying Pan","paragraphs":["‘Curse it all!'","As the wind howled and the endless bolts of lightning scorched the sky, a ferocious mass of dark clouds churning like a celestial ocean, the Night Garden plummeted toward the ground. At first, Nightwalker simply meant to descend below the clouds to shield his warriors from the rising moon — but now, the living ship was wounded too severely to be controlled, and its fall had become unstoppable.","Of course, the titanic creature holding it in a crushing grip was not helping the situation either.","The hull of the great vessel was slowly devouring its flesh, but the damn abomination was too vast and too powerful — there were fractures slowly appearing on the miraculous wood already, and the damage being dealt to the Night Garden was far beyond what the living ship could return.","Usually, slamming into the ground would not have been a major concern. However, with the ship already damaged, a collision could very well become catastrophic — not to mention that the impact would devastate countless districts of NQSC.","The Night Garden was a dozen kilometers from stern to bow, after all, and its mass was incalculable. The speed of its fall looked deceptively tame because of its size, but in truth, it was dire.","Nightwalker couldn't right the ship with the damn Titan weighing it down, though. Sinking his colossal, ethereal fangs into the flesh of the monster, he tore off an enormous chunk of flesh and bellowed, his eerie voice drowning out the deafening roars of the storm.","His Transcendent form, the Starbeast, was uncanny and immensely powerful. However, one thing it did not possess was vocal cords capable of human speech... it was alright, though. Because Aether could understand him.","So, what Nightwalker was relaying to his warriors was quite simple:","“Aether! Concentrate on its right shoulder joint! Take its remaining wing off!\"","Almost immediately, the soldiers below rushed to turn the cannons. Some were crawling across the deck, dazed by the terrifying presence of the Titan... some were dead, having been turned into bloody stains. But no one had abandoned their duty. Nightwalker's Saints were all going all out to free their ship from the abomination’s grasp, as well.","But it was not going to be enough.","Perched on the creature's endless back and rending it to shreds with his ethereal fangs, Nightwalker could see the ground clearly. The devastated landscape of the abandoned battlefield beyond the walls of NQSC was drawing closer and closer.","They were not going to kill the Titan in time. They were not even going to sever its one remaining wing in time.","Even with Nightwalker expanding space to extend the calamitous fall, it was not enough — the world he was trying to reshape with his Will was permeated by the Will of the colossal Nightmare Creature, after all, slowing him down.","\"Goddammit!\"","Looking up, Nightwalker hesitated for a moment, then turned into a torrent of starlight and flashed toward the scarred and battered Mainmast Pagoda. Once inside, he slid across the floor of the runic hall and jumped to his feet, bending space to enter the runic circle in one step.","There, Naeve was standing on one knee, blood streaming down his face. The runic hall had sustained severe damage, but luckily enough, the circle itself was intact — steering the living ship without it was not impossible, but quite difficult.","\"Grab the rails!\"","Nightwalker's voice boomed across the entire main deck of the titanic vessel, sending the soldiers scurrying to grab something as if their lives depended on it. The Night Garden was supposed to keep them firmly standing on the deck no matter what maneuvers its helmsman had in mind, but with how damaged it was, there was no telling what would happen.","There was nothing to grab onto in the runic hall, though, so Naeve simply grabbed onto the belt of Nightwalker's armor.","The Night Garden careened, its bow moments away from crashing into the ground...","But just before it could, an enormous fissure opened in the fabric of reality, revealing an endless black void that was illuminated by countless stars and dreamlike nebulas.","The bow of the living ship plunged into the Dream Gate, which had opened parallel to the ground. The colossal fissure swallowed the entire great length of the Night Garden — from the runic hall, it looked as if they were falling into the starlit sky.","Then, the Mainmast Pagoda crossed the Dream Gate, as well.","A moment later, Nightwalker was blinded by brilliant light.","He was assaulted by unbearable heat.","The howling cacophony of the endless storm disappeared, replaced by a deafening litany of countless monstrous wails.","When Nightwalker's eyes adjusted to the light, what he saw...","Was a world on fire.","The Night Garden had exited the Dream Gate upside-down, momentum taking it higher into the azure sky. It was already spinning to right itself, but for now, all Nightwalker could see was the ground — the vast expanse of a sandy desert, all of it drowning in an ocean of silver flame. Myriads of Nightmare Creatures were moving in that flame, the black fractures of Nightmare Gates towering above them like dark pillars.","The air was full of winged abominations as well, all of them fusing into a harrowing swarm. Far in the distance, a battered city was unleashing a hail of explosive rounds into the swarm, streams of tracer rounds twisting like radiant snakes.","The terrifying sight was like a scene from hell... but it wasn't some distant inferno. The Night Garden gave Nightwalker the ability to open his Dream Gate between two points in the same realm, and that was what he had done, bringing his ship to the Western Quadrant.","They were currently in the Sahara Desert, where the forces of humanity were fighting a desperate battle against the advancing tide of abominations.","The hull of the Night Garden cracked precariously as the Titan tightened its coils, and since the titanic ship appeared right in the middle of a great swarm of winged abominations, those monsters were shifting their attention to its vast expanse as well. Nightwalker gritted his teeth.","“All battle crew below Transcendent Rank! Kill the vermin! Don't let a single bastard land!\"","As the Night Garden spun, aligning its main mast with the boundless sky above, the soldiers let go of the rails and unleashed a squall of attacks at the churning swarm. The Saints, meanwhile, kept attacking the Titan. Nightwalker swayed as the colossal creature's claws tore into the Mainmast Pagoda, then cursed and gazed at the swarming sky outside...","And there, he saw what he was looking for, moving like an annihilating shadow in the endless mass of abominations.","A great dragon with scales the color of the midnight sky was reigning terror in the sky above the ocean of flames, carving a path of destruction through the swarm. As Nightwalker watched, its enormous maw opened, and a haunting song resounded above the endless battlefield.","In the next moment, a blinding pillar of silver flame incinerated countless Nightmare Creatures, plunging toward the ground and cleaving a deadly path through the horde of abominations attacking the city.","Thousands of them were slaughtered in an instant, and more still perished as the dragon moved its head, sending the beam of silver death rolling across the desert. The sand boiled, turning into molten lava and flowing like a fiery sea.","Even if the dragon was too far for Nightwalker to see its eyes, he suddenly felt a heavy gaze crushing into him.","Smiling crookedly, he waved and then pointed to the enormous Titan strangling the ship.","The dragon studied him for a few moments and then changed course, moving swiftly in the direction of the Night Garden. Nightwalker let out a tired sigh, then laughed.","\"Damn it. Is his shift not over yet? I hoped to meet one of the young ladies instead...\"","Then, he helped Naeve to his feet, patted him on the shoulder, and turned into a stream of starlight again.","By the time Kai arrived, he was already rending the Titan's flesh. The Starbeast attacked the colossal abomination from the left, while the dragon descended upon it from the right like a dark mass of celestial fury.","Soon enough, rivers of blood flowed onto the deck of the Night Garden.","...An hour later, the Titan was dead. The swarm of winged abominations had been repelled, and the horde of Nightmare Creatures on the ground had turned to ash. The enemy was not defeated, but it was pushed back, for now — for a few days, or perhaps hours.","Or perhaps even minutes.","In the endless chaos of the end of days, nobody could say for sure.","Nightwalker was inspecting the damage when Kai landed on the bloody deck beside him, having already assumed his human form. The young man looked quite stunning, but also tired and grim — there were bruises under his eyes, and his skin was smeared with soot and dried blood.","Looking around, he grimaced.","“How bad is it?\"","Nightwalker cursed.","“Quite bad. The Night Garden is grievously wounded... I think I'll need to spend at least a few weeks at the wharf Lady Ananke built.\"","Needless to say, with the Night Garden disappearing for several weeks, the situation in the waking world was bound to turn from bad to worse.","Kai sighed.","\"Effie can cover for some of it... I'll talk to her.\"","Then, he closed his eyes for a moment, suppressing a groan.","When he opened them again, Nightwalker could already see that their conversation would be cut short.","Kai took a step back and nodded.","“I cannot stay any longer. Do not linger either — stay safe.\"","Saying that, Kai threw one last look at the devastated deck of the Night Garden and pulled himself across the realm boundary.","A few heartbeats later, the unbearable strike of the vast desert, a great swath of it turned to glass, was replaced by unbearable cold. The winds howled, throwing sharp ice crystals into his face. The air smelled of blood and ash, and he was plunged into the clamor of battle once more.","Kai sighed and looked ahead.","In front of him were the spires of the Jade Palace, and beyond them, on the plain below the mountains, a great blizzard was devouring the world. He could see the shapes of countless snow wraiths moving under the cover of the blizzard, and the banners of Seishan's legion fluttering in the wind like a river of blood.","With his miraculous sight, he saw it all — Seishan and her sisters, their Transcendent champions, Ascended officers, Awakened soldiers, Beastmaster's thralls shielding the humans with their bodies, countless Echoes throwing themselves into the mass of enemies, the Ravenous Fiend moving through the blizzard like an obliterating mountain of fire and steel...","Mundane soldiers were manning the fortifications that protected the city, and more Awakened were bracing themselves as the towering, churning white wall of the blizzard drew closer to the vast expanse of scarlet fields.","He also saw three colossal shapes moving far in the distance, guiding the blizzard like profane shepherds. Each of them was tall enough to dwarf mountains and eerie enough to make even his blood run cold. Kai inhaled deeply and summoned his bow.","“It just never ends, does it?\"","He nocked an arrow and launched himself into the swirling snow.","Then again, perhaps it was good that the battle never ended.","Life was war, after all.","The day all fighting ceased would be the day all humans were gone.","For now, though, they were still here.","They were still fighting."]}]);
